From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonid <leonidy.1985@yandex.ru>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:40:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: it6112: WIP - move 212 lines of vblank into the
 back porch

The panel shows the frame ~212 lines early: with the vendor porches
(vsa 8, vbp 28, vfp 220) a ~10% black band sits on the portrait top edge
and the opposite edge is cut off, at boot as well as in the compositor,
so it is not a userspace problem.

First experiment: keep vsa 8 and move the 212 lines from the front porch
into the back porch (vbp 240, vfp 8).  The vblank total stays 256 lines,
so the pixel clock is untouched.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-it6112-boe-tv110xum-lb2.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-it6112-boe-tv110xum-lb2.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-it6112-boe-tv110xum-lb2.c
index d3082865b..e23dc351a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-it6112-boe-tv110xum-lb2.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-it6112-boe-tv110xum-lb2.c
@@ -902,9 +902,16 @@ static const struct drm_display_mode boe_tv110xum_lb2_mode = {
 	.hsync_end = 1600 + 14 + 44,
 	.htotal = 1600 + 14 + 44 + 44,
 	.vdisplay = 2176,
+	/*
+	 * EXPERIMENT: the image comes out shifted towards the start of the
+	 * frame - a ~10% black band on the portrait top edge, content cut off
+	 * on the opposite edge - so move ~212 lines from the front porch into
+	 * the back porch.  The vblank total (and the pixel clock) is unchanged,
+	 * so this only moves the active window inside the frame.
+	 */
 	.vsync_start = 2176 + 8,
-	.vsync_end = 2176 + 8 + 28,
-	.vtotal = 2176 + 8 + 28 + 220,
+	.vsync_end = 2176 + 8 + 240,
+	.vtotal = 2176 + 8 + 240 + 8,
 	.width_mm = 166,
 	.height_mm = 226,
 };
